From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 13:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec/decode: one thread for a V4L2 request decoder

A V4L2 request decoder decodes in hardware, and one thread already keeps
it fed: H.264 and HEVC hand out their frames in display order, behind
the next request. Frame threads only pass frames between them and wait
on the request context's one mutex. On an RK3528 at 3840x2160, HEVC
decodes at 113.4 fps on one thread and 105.1 at the automatic count,
H.264 at 60.1 and 58.6; Rockchip's MPP decoder, never frame threaded,
at 115.8 and 61.3.

Where the caller leaves the thread count to FFmpeg and hands the decoder
a V4L2 request device, decode on one thread. A count the caller sets is
kept.
---
diff --git a/libavcodec/decode.c b/libavcodec/decode.c
index ba6ff8a..29ded4c 100644
--- a/libavcodec/decode.c
+++ b/libavcodec/decode.c
@@ -2039,6 +2039,14 @@ av_cold int ff_decode_preinit(AVCodecContext *avctx)
             dc->initial_pict_type = AV_PICTURE_TYPE_I;
     }
 
+    /* A V4L2 request decoder decodes in hardware: frame threads only hand
+     * frames between them and wait on its one context. Left to choose, it
+     * decodes on one thread. */
+    if (!avctx->thread_count && avctx->hw_device_ctx &&
+        ((AVHWDeviceContext *)avctx->hw_device_ctx->data)->type ==
+            AV_HWDEVICE_TYPE_V4L2REQUEST)
+        avctx->thread_count = 1;
+
     /* if the decoder init function was already called previously,
      * free the already allocated subtitle_header before overwriting it */
     av_freep(&avctx->subtitle_header);
